WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.860
Two great armies face each
other across a battlefield.

2
00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.700
Between them stands a single chariot.

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.170
In it is Arjuna, a great archer.

4
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.680
Across the field he sees his
teachers, his uncles, his cousins.

5
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.240
He drops his bow.

6
00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.760
He will not kill his own family.

7
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:23.130
His charioteer is Krishna, whom
many Hindus worship as God.

8
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.520
So why does Krishna tell him to stand up?

9
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.300
In this mission, you'll read Krishna's
answer in the Song of the Lord,

10
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.470
part of a vast epic.

11
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.810
Then you'll explore three
paths that the song teaches:

12
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.770
action, knowledge and devotion.

13
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: find out why Krishna
tells Arjuna to stand up and fight.
